machine_text:
A straggling few got up to go in deep despair. The rest
Clung to the hope which springs eternal in the human breast;
They thought, if only future wormhole could get a whack at that -
We'd put up even money, now. 

There was ease in future wormhole's manner as they stepped into their place;
There was pride in future wormhole’s bearing and a smile on future wormhole's face.
And when, responding to the cheers, they lightly doffed their hat,
No stranger in the crowd could doubt 'twas future wormhole at the bat.

Ten thousand eyes were on them as they rubbed their hands with dust;
Five thousand tongues applauded when they wiped them on their space-suit.
And while the sneering Susie ground the ball into her hip,
Defiance gleamed in future wormhole’s eye, a sneer curled future wormhole’s lip.

And now the cosmic ball came hurtling through the air,
And future wormhole stood a-watching it in haughty grandeur there.
Close by the sturdy batsman the ball unheeded sped-
"That ain't my style," said future wormhole. "Strike one," the umpire said.

From the benches, black with people, there went up a muffled roar,
Like the beating of the storm-waves on a stern and distant shore;
"Kill them, kill the umpire!" shouted someone on the stand;
And it's likely they'd have killed them had not future wormhole raised their hand.

With a smile of Christian charity great future wormhole’s visage shone;
They stilled the rising tumult; they bade the game go on;
They signaled to the pitcher, and once more the spheroid flew;
But future wormhole still ignored it, and the umpire said, "Strike two."

Now future wormhole’s face grew stern, they frowned in great disdain,
And still defiantly they stood, they quivered, full of strain.
And once more threw Susie; and now the ball did shiver,
But future wormhole swung the bat, and the crowd exploded in a quiver. 

Oh, somewhere in this favored land the sun is shining bright;
The band is playing somewhere, and somewhere hearts are light,
And somewhere men are laughing, and somewhere children shout;
But there is no joy in Frizzlesnapville - mighty future wormhole has struck out.
